  "explanation": [
    "Store originals and thumbnails in object storage and serve them through a CDN with long cache lifetimes: images never change once uploaded.",
    "Uploads go straight to storage (presigned URLs) and a queue triggers thumbnail generation.",
    "Keep only small metadata in the database and cache it: page views then barely touch the backend."
  ]
